														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3821391">
									

<p>For me, this comes across as pretty profound in and of itself. I've never seen an SCP document that explores and &quot;anomalizes&quot; the Veil.</p>
<p>In their increasingly complex attempts to put a wall between what's normal and what isn't, the Foundation are now in a peculiar situation where <em>the wall itself is becoming abnormal</em>. I've never seen anything like this, and if something similar's been done, it doesn't stick out as much as <em>this</em> does.</p>
<p>The now-anomalous concept of the Veil is getting difficult for both civilians and Foundation personnel to pass through safely, and rubbing up <em>against</em> the Veil, either through Foundation personnel coming into contact with normalcy or vice versa, has the potential to cause strange side effects that must themselves be contained, which makes the Veil <em>more</em> anomalous and more difficult to handle, which causes more side effects, which must also be contained, and so on and so on, ad infinitum.</p>
<p>At some point, this leaning wall has to tip over. And what that entails, I have no idea.</p>
<p>But I'm <em>dying</em> to find out. +1</p>

							</div>

								
					
