<p>Novote. I want to like this because I love explorations of the Foundation being just incomprehensibly controlling toward humanity, but for most of the same reasons TL333's mentioned, it just falls flat by the end for me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Addressing SCP-3475 as a single whole allows for the greatest degree of control over civilian populations and allows side effects to be dealt with more easily. The SCP-3475 program currently allows civilian humanity to enjoy the greatest possible degree of normalcy and stability in spite of anomalous threats.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is the part that really makes me think this is more fitting for an 001 designation.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Soon after introduction, the most common species of <strong>canids became increasingly difficult to perceive,</strong> and as such this issue has been made inconsequential.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a very specific topic similarity to what we posted several days ago for our DoomCon stuff. That said, the idea that the Foundation engineered this particular abnormality and then disguised it as a Lethe Event could be interesting, too, and is what my brain came up with as an explanation when I read this and noticed the overlap.</p>

							</div>

								
					
